     [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 5 +                                                                                                                                                                    [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 6 +[38;2;248;248;242mClarified in the session: the phone is a **Xiaomi Redmi 15C**, running Metro as the **installed                                                                     [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 7 +[38;2;248;248;242mapp (PWA)**. The sheet ended cleanly after 3 rows, while another phone at the same time showed more                                                                 [K[m            [38;2;80;200;80m[48;2;2;40;0m 8 +[38;2;248;248;242mthan 4 buses heading to the stop.                                                                                                                                   [K[m       [38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Allowed by auto mode classifier                                                                                                                                                [m                                                                                                                                                                                    [38;2;255;255;255m● [mI've made a fix on a new branch, [38;2;177;185;249m007-sheet-improvements-fix[m, but I couldn't test it on a Redmi 15C, so please check it on the phone. Nothing is committed yet.                                                                                                                                                                                                          [1mCause:[22m the sheet always has room for 4 rows, on every screen size. The problem is that the app told the browser it could draw behind the phone's system bars ([38;2;177;185;249mviewport-fit=cover[m).  It then relied on the phone reporting how tall the navigation bar is ([38;2;177;185;249menv(safe-area-inset-bottom)[m) so it could keep the sheet above it. If a phone reports 0 but still covers the   bottom of the page, the 4th row ends up under the navigation bar. The sheet and the bar are both white, so it looks like the list just ends after 3 rows. The installed app on    
  newer Android versions draws edge to edge, which fits that. This is my best explanation, not something I confirmed on the device.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       [1mFix:[22m[K
